From: underdone
Subject: [PATCH] virtualhid: honour the non-normalized key code flag on the uinput path

Moonlight marks JIS-specific keys (yen, ro, kana, henkan, muhenkan) with
SS_KBE_FLAG_NON_NORMALIZED so the host can translate them by physical
position. The virtualhid path already forwarded the flag; the uinput
fallback path dropped it, so those keys never reached libvirtualhid as
layout-native key codes.

This patch is part of a JIS (Japanese keyboard) support change set.
License: GPL-3.0-or-later, matching LizardByte/Sunshine.

--- a/src/platform/virtualhid_input.cpp
+++ b/src/platform/virtualhid_input.cpp
@@ -314,7 +314,7 @@ namespace platf::virtualhid {
       event.uses_normalized_key_code = (static_cast<std::byte>(flags) & static_cast<std::byte>(SS_KBE_FLAG_NON_NORMALIZED)) == std::byte {};
       event.prefer_native_scan_code = config::input.always_send_scancodes;
 #else
-      (void) flags;
+      event.uses_normalized_key_code = (static_cast<std::byte>(flags) & static_cast<std::byte>(SS_KBE_FLAG_NON_NORMALIZED)) == std::byte {};
 #endif
       return event;
     }
